Z||000003||TwisT||02-05-2001||07:54 PM||||That DOES look sweet and I've always wondered how feasable it would be to do it.  Looks wicked,  but then you have the panel-removal thing.  It leaves me wondering...  <P>Why not?<P>If a person went through all the work of painting their Fiero anyway,  and spent a little extra time filling and smoothing the seams,  what would it hurt?  Sure you couldn't just whip a body-panel off at will...  but who needs to?  Also...  if you were to get into a wreck,  your pannel is screwed-up anyway.  You may indeed have to spend a little extra dough to get it smoothed back to original,  but I think it wouldn't be too big of a deal.  I think using fiberglass mat would be the material of choice.<P>Maybe I'm just blowing some hot air through my blow-hole.  Heh he heee...<P>Maybe some more experienced body men can fill us in on this.  I know I would like to know how good/ bad this would be,  as I've thought about doing it myself.<BR>||||reg||1
